meta {
  name: payment testing
}

docs {
  # Payment testing collection

  Standalone, end-to-end test of the tab / Stripe authorize-then-capture flow.
  Run with the Bruno runner in `seq` order (or fire requests top to bottom);
  later requests reuse runtime vars (`bru.setVar`) set by earlier ones.

  IMPORTANT: select the **Dev** environment before running, otherwise
  `{{host}}` / `{{port}}` are empty and the URLs are invalid.

  ## Why the Stripe "confirm" steps exist
  Checkout calls the real `stripe.paymentIntents.capture()`. Simulating our own
  webhook only flips the TabPayment to AUTHORIZED in our DB; on Stripe's side the
  PaymentIntent is still unconfirmed and not capturable, so checkout would 500.
  Each hold that gets captured is therefore first confirmed against the real
  Stripe test API with `pm_card_visa` (requests 03, 07, 13), which drives it to
  `requires_capture`. The webhook simulation is still needed to update our DB,
  because Stripe cannot reach localhost without the Stripe CLI.

  Prerequisites:
  - Dev env: `eventId` is an ACTIVE event with `standId` / `productId` under it;
    product price well below the EUR 10.00 (1000 cents) baseline hold.
  - `stripeSecretKey` (Dev env) is the project's Stripe TEST secret key.
  - Backend runs in dev (`nodeEnv !== "production"`) so /webhooks/stripe accepts
    unsigned JSON.

  ## Happy path (seq 1-11)
  1  create attendee session
  2  create tab                   -> baseline hold (PENDING)
  3  confirm baseline PI (Stripe) -> requires_capture
  4  webhook authorize baseline   -> DB AUTHORIZED, tab OPEN
  5  order under limit            -> 201, items released (proves baseline auth)
  6  order over limit             -> 402, overage hold created, items gated
  7  confirm overage PI (Stripe)  -> requires_capture
  8  webhook authorize overage    -> DB AUTHORIZED, gated items released
  9  webhook replay baseline      -> idempotency no-op (still 200)
  10 checkout tab                 -> captures baseline + overage, tab PAID
  11 cancel paid order            -> 409 (guard: paid order cannot be cancelled)

  ## Failure path (seq 12-17)
  12 create tab (failure flow)
  13 confirm baseline 2 PI (Stripe)
  14 webhook authorize baseline 2
  15 order over limit 2           -> 402 (overage left UNconfirmed on Stripe)
  16 webhook payment_failed       -> overage hold FAILED, tab reopened
  17 checkout tab 2               -> captures baseline ONLY (1000 cents), proving
     the failed overage was never captured

  ## Known gap
  The positive cancel case (200 + gated items cancelled) is not covered: the 402
  response does not return the gated order id and there is no list-orders
  endpoint, so the test cannot address the gated order. Request 11 exercises only
  the guard.
}
